53:34.992 --> 53:38.733
outside. Um, and they're also— they've

53:39.233 --> 53:42.315
already spent down all that money in terms of work. We haven't reimbursed them yet.

53:42.379 --> 53:45.992
But yeah, that's the current year. And then this

53:46.492 --> 53:49.959
bottom portion is just kind of a general overview of what is eligible.

53:50.585 --> 53:54.199
So overall, for CDBG, um, the funds

53:54.699 --> 53:58.583
are just meant to benefit low-to-moderate income people. What that looks like

53:58.663 --> 54:02.020
is for every project, at least 51% of people served

54:02.293 --> 54:05.714
must be 80% AMI or under, if that makes

54:05.746 --> 54:09.425
sense. So 2 percentages there, but basically at least

54:09.925 --> 54:12.622
51% of people served for each project have to be low to moderate income.

54:13.538 --> 54:16.799
And you can keep track of that in various ways.

54:17.297 --> 54:20.495
We get into it more in the packet, but like for public service, we have

54:20.527 --> 54:24.070
to check income for every single person that benefits from the service.

54:24.119 --> 54:27.788
And then for things like the ADA ramps, you know, we'd have

54:27.820 --> 54:30.979
