01:53:19.306 --> 01:53:23.562
see something that says this is going to be $200 million or

01:53:23.660 --> 01:53:27.044
$220 million or has the potential to be those things.

01:53:27.499 --> 01:53:30.900
So the thing that I would ask is, as you start to

01:53:31.400 --> 01:53:35.113
see these things and posts that people put up. If you have questions, reach out

01:53:35.613 --> 01:53:38.377
to us. All of our contact info is on the city website. We're happy to

01:53:38.409 --> 01:53:40.866
answer some of the questions and the things that we're thinking about with it,

01:53:41.319 --> 01:53:44.859
and we're even more happy to receive your guys's feedback when it

01:53:45.359 --> 01:53:48.840
comes to items like the things that we have on our agenda. So thank

01:53:48.874 --> 01:53:49.632
you all for being here.

01:53:53.598 --> 01:53:57.463
Welcome and thank you to our first responders and our second responders.

01:53:57.513 --> 01:54:01.058
You guys will get to decide who's who. I'm not going to enter into that

01:54:01.187 --> 01:54:05.040
fight. I'm just glad you're all here. Just express my

01:54:05.540 --> 01:54:08.537
gratitude to the citizens of Eagle Mountain for the opportunity to sit in this seat

01:54:09.187 --> 01:54:12.701
and to listen, to hear, and to make decisions

01:54:12.750 --> 01:54:16.024
on your behalf. And I would just reiterate what Councilmember Clark

01:54:16.524 --> 01:54:21.021
said. Our phone numbers are published on the website. We're pretty much— we

01:54:21.521 --> 01:54:24.759
cannot escape your input, and we don't want to. We need it and

01:54:25.259 --> 01:54:28.937
want it. So please reach out to us and ask us questions. To have

01:54:29.437 --> 01:54:33.180
a conversation one-on-one is so much more beneficial in my mind than it is

01:54:33.373 --> 01:54:36.481
to throw innuendo and wonder and

01:54:36.577 --> 01:54:40.055
make supposition. When you really take the time to engage

01:54:40.555 --> 01:54:43.602
with one of us, you'll find that we're not quite the noobs that you think

01:54:44.102 --> 01:54:46.679
we are. At least I hope that's what you find. Or you may find that

01:54:47.179 --> 01:54:50.806
we are the noobs that you think we are. at least have some background

01:54:51.306 --> 01:54:55.462
and some understanding that perhaps you haven't been allowed to hear or see. And we're

01:54:55.527 --> 01:54:59.091
happy to help you understand what we see and what we're concerned

01:54:59.591 --> 01:55:02.752
about. Eagle Mountain is the best city in the state of Utah. There's no question

01:55:03.252 --> 01:55:06.060
about that. So I'm sorry for those of you that don't live here. But Councilmember

01:55:06.560 --> 01:55:09.351
Clark told me just to remind you that we do have a mortgage assistance program

01:55:09.851 --> 01:55:12.884
for first responders. So the more of you that want to come live out here,

01:55:13.028 --> 01:55:15.245
you know, you don't have to work. You don't necessarily have to be You could

01:55:15.745 --> 01:55:17.343
be here every day, but you could come and live with us as well,

01:55:17.440 --> 01:55:20.378
and we invite you to do that. So thank you to the mayor and the

01:55:20.878 --> 01:55:23.768
council members for their, their hard work, and for our staff, and for all that

01:55:23.784 --> 01:55:26.767
they do to help us enjoy the measure of success that we do.

01:55:30.339 --> 01:55:33.803
It's interesting, I had some thoughts prepared, and, uh,

01:55:35.172 --> 01:55:38.009
these prior 2 council members already shared some of what I was about to share.

01:55:38.075 --> 01:55:43.128
So I'm just going to reiterate this, that there's a principle

01:55:43.628 --> 01:55:46.610
in life that Stephen Covey taught about seeking first to understand before seeking to be

01:55:47.110 --> 01:55:50.696
understood. And sitting now in this chair where I was sitting

01:55:50.856 --> 01:55:54.654
in that chair just a few weeks ago and having

01:55:55.154 --> 01:55:58.388
spent numerous hours already serving in this capacity,

01:55:59.093 --> 01:56:02.795
meeting with different entities that

01:56:03.295 --> 01:56:06.609
are— that have interests here in the city, whether it's developers or landowners,

01:56:09.637 --> 01:56:12.861
businesses. Doing— going through that process helps provide a

01:56:12.973 --> 01:56:16.503
more understanding, and then that helps hopefully

01:56:17.003 --> 01:56:20.464
sharpen the decisions that we make. And it's just interesting when I, you know,

01:56:20.512 --> 01:56:23.388
occasionally will look on Facebook and see comments from citizens.

01:56:24.079 --> 01:56:27.694
It's evident when some citizens

01:56:28.194 --> 01:56:30.803
talk and they don't have all the details on the table. And so I echo

01:56:31.303 --> 01:56:34.576
the sentiments of Councilmember Clark and Councilmember Wright that If you have

01:56:35.588 --> 01:56:38.863
a concern about something that's so significant that you're ready to lead others in a

01:56:39.363 --> 01:56:43.214
cause about it, come talk first and see what information we have. You may

01:56:43.294 --> 01:56:46.891
still feel that your position is right and you should still have a voice and

01:56:47.228 --> 01:56:50.038
lead people against something that you feel is not correct.

01:56:51.081 --> 01:56:55.272
But I would encourage coming and actually getting as many details as possible before

01:56:55.721 --> 01:56:59.013
trying to lead others down a certain pathway. You might

01:56:59.513 --> 01:57:03.603
be surprised about the details and information that you'll learn in that process that

01:57:04.103 --> 01:57:07.696
may change the way you approach things. And I'll tell you that sitting

01:57:07.760 --> 01:57:10.986
in this chair has given me a lot of additional perspective I didn't have previously.

01:57:11.772 --> 01:57:14.468
And I comment to my wife, I say,

01:57:15.158 --> 01:57:18.416
you know, it's interesting when you try to judge

01:57:18.432 --> 01:57:21.723
what a puzzle is when you don't have all the puzzle pieces to look at.

01:57:23.006 --> 01:57:26.569
And as sitting in this perspective here, gives us some

01:57:27.069 --> 01:57:30.708
additional puzzle pieces. You also bring additional puzzle pieces that we

01:57:31.208 --> 01:57:34.350
may not have, and it's really critical for us to hear from what your perspective

01:57:34.850 --> 01:57:37.943
is and what you're experiencing. So we definitely need to hear from you.

01:57:38.809 --> 01:57:41.280
We have our own perspectives we bring, but we need to hear yours as well.

01:57:41.954 --> 01:57:45.659
And we will have a more— a stronger city if

01:57:45.708 --> 01:57:49.558
we can collaborate one with another and in

01:57:50.058 --> 01:57:53.568
a respectful fashion where we get as much information from each other as possible

01:57:54.547 --> 01:57:57.740
instead of trying to voice a viewpoint without having heard the other side just

01:57:58.240 --> 01:58:02.601
yet. That's an important principle in life and something I teach in

01:58:02.745 --> 01:58:06.018
my company. I teach the values of love, serve,

01:58:06.082 --> 01:58:10.478
connect, and transform as some of the more important

01:58:10.750 --> 01:58:14.970
principles that you can follow to have a successful organization. It's challenging

01:58:15.002 --> 01:58:18.628
for us to connect as citizens when we're not willing to

01:58:18.676 --> 01:58:22.283
listen to one another first before vocalizing our own opinion.

01:58:22.718 --> 01:58:25.987
And so it's my hope that we can remember those principles, and I'm saying this

01:58:26.260 --> 01:58:30.017
to myself as well, to remember these principles, that we can

01:58:30.518 --> 01:58:33.859
listen to others first and seek to hear their viewpoints

01:58:34.408 --> 01:58:36.151
before trying to vocalize our own.

01:58:39.453 --> 01:58:43.100
Yeah, I just want to echo everything that was said previously. One of the quotes

01:58:43.165 --> 01:58:46.974
that has been coming to mind to me recently is, if you If

01:58:47.474 --> 01:58:49.944
you want a smaller government, you need a bigger people.

01:58:51.052 --> 01:58:54.665
And when I first heard that, I thought, okay, that means I need to lift

01:58:55.165 --> 01:58:59.177
where I'm where I'm standing in my own community. So I love

01:58:59.257 --> 01:59:02.372
when citizens come and they bring things like this. You know,

01:59:02.388 --> 01:59:06.483
they're digging through 2006 Planning Commission

01:59:06.983 --> 01:59:10.497
notes to figure out how how was my HOA formed? What are the next steps

01:59:10.997 --> 01:59:14.841
that I can take? I joked earlier in our working

01:59:14.889 --> 01:59:18.001
session that if you remember the movie

01:59:18.034 --> 01:59:21.275
Field of Dreams, there's this line, if you build

01:59:21.775 --> 01:59:25.474
it, they will come. And in Eagle Mountain, we all came, and now we're

01:59:25.974 --> 01:59:29.497
trying to build it. We're trying to get the infrastructure and the roads and,

01:59:30.370 --> 01:59:34.213
you know, the proper staffing and all of those things. So we're

01:59:34.325 --> 01:59:37.622
playing a lot of catch-up. And, you know, as Councilmember

01:59:38.122 --> 01:59:41.594
Whiting said, I'm sorry. You're— you kind of see the top part of the iceberg,

01:59:41.610 --> 01:59:44.967
and once you get into this role, you are learning about the other 90%

01:59:45.208 --> 01:59:48.870
that's just not obvious. So I

01:59:48.886 --> 01:59:52.195
appreciate the opportunity to serve and look forward

01:59:52.695 --> 01:59:56.033
to our discussion today. Thank you, Mayor. Yep,

01:59:56.114 --> 01:59:59.503
thanks guys. And I just want to add my appreciation.

01:59:59.583 --> 02:00:03.213
Definitely talking about different roles, when I

02:00:03.713 --> 02:00:07.082
stepped into this seat It's a little bit different than what

02:00:07.582 --> 02:00:10.740
I'm used to, and especially thanks to our first and second responders. And we'll

02:00:11.240 --> 02:00:14.285
let you arm wrestle that, but we'll decide who wins at the rodeo and the

02:00:14.350 --> 02:00:16.246
goat tying or whatever, right? So,

02:00:17.901 --> 02:00:21.114
but definitely thanks. And in this role, I get to kind of get in the

02:00:21.614 --> 02:00:24.478
trenches a little bit more and spend a lot of time with both staff and,

02:00:25.077 --> 02:00:28.477
and all of our department heads and whatnot. It's a pleasure to be in the

02:00:28.977 --> 02:00:32.014
trench doing the heavy lifting with, with you guys. And all of our staff members.

02:00:32.062 --> 02:00:35.707
It's been an honor. So just want to add my gratitude

02:00:36.462 --> 02:00:39.914
and thanks to as well the council who put up with me and take my

02:00:40.414 --> 02:00:43.591
calls all the time to try to get through some of this lift

02:00:44.091 --> 02:00:46.497
that we have in front of us. So let's get right to it.

