03:22:08.072 --> 03:22:11.982
In the actual language of the, uh, of the

03:22:12.159 --> 03:22:15.492
bond parameters resolution, it's really outlining that this is

03:22:15.524 --> 03:22:18.296
for water and wastewater enhancements,

03:22:19.129 --> 03:22:22.527
but those are the, the intended 3 projects that we would use the funds for.

03:22:23.696 --> 03:22:28.856
The bond parameters resolution also establishes the anticipated

03:22:29.356 --> 03:22:32.441
anticipated maximum bond amount, the maximum possible interest rate,

03:22:33.003 --> 03:22:36.792
maximum duration, par amounts, and whatnot. So basically it's

03:22:36.921 --> 03:22:40.533
the parameters by which we would operate. At this early

03:22:41.033 --> 03:22:44.965
stage in the process, we are still working to refine the costs on our

03:22:45.465 --> 03:22:49.076
sewer treatment project. It's also— we're also in the design phase,

03:22:49.204 --> 03:22:53.507
and in fact the council just a few minutes ago approved funding

03:22:53.620 --> 03:22:57.731
for the design of the East Trunk Line, and so we appreciate that.

03:22:58.197 --> 03:23:01.843
So all of those costs are under refinement, but we have high-level engineers'

03:23:01.971 --> 03:23:05.890
estimates that we have included in this, along with contingency

03:23:06.002 --> 03:23:09.777
to ensure that the bond parameters resolution is going to be large enough to

03:23:10.277 --> 03:23:13.952
ensure that we can move forward with these projects. But we

03:23:14.452 --> 03:23:18.112
anticipate the actual cost to come in much lower. The reason we

03:23:18.128 --> 03:23:21.741
want to start early in the process of having a bond parameters

03:23:22.241 --> 03:23:25.595
resolution is not only one, to engage the public and allow them to

03:23:26.095 --> 03:23:28.918
come to a public hearing and participate in that process,

03:23:29.609 --> 03:23:32.884
but also two, we want to ensure that we have the

03:23:33.125 --> 03:23:37.444
best possible cost and the least likelihood

03:23:37.621 --> 03:23:41.860
of project schedule delays by being able to order long

03:23:41.972 --> 03:23:46.918
lead time items early, such as transformers

03:23:47.094 --> 03:23:50.290
or the membranes in the membrane bioreactor, those things that

03:23:50.322 --> 03:23:53.629
would take upwards of a year to 2 years to acquire, we want to make

03:23:54.129 --> 03:23:57.338
sure that we get those ordered at the lowest possible price, which is today's price,

03:23:57.949 --> 03:24:01.545
and we get those coming and they're on hand so that when the project

03:24:02.045 --> 03:24:05.463
does move forward, we can, one, make sure that we have them and

03:24:05.963 --> 03:24:08.546
it's not going to cause any scheduling delays, and two,

03:24:09.108 --> 03:24:12.239
that that we

03:24:12.739 --> 03:24:16.220
can reimburse ourselves for those purchases out of future bond

03:24:16.253 --> 03:24:20.266
proceeds. Part of this bond parameters resolution anticipates

03:24:20.766 --> 03:24:24.376
that we would use bond proceeds to be able to pay for those hard costs.

03:24:24.826 --> 03:24:28.230
Without such a resolution in place, we would only be

03:24:28.730 --> 03:24:33.817
able to reimburse ourselves for design costs. So that's the general high-level

03:24:33.897 --> 03:24:36.289
view of what a bond parameters resolution is.

03:24:38.608 --> 03:24:42.744
Involves. We will continue to work on refining

03:24:42.857 --> 03:24:45.882
the costs involved. Like I said, we will continue to work on

03:24:46.156 --> 03:24:49.620
looking for grants and low-interest or zero-interest loans that

03:24:50.120 --> 03:24:53.439
we can put towards this. Of course, we have to go through a process

03:24:53.568 --> 03:24:57.618
to become bond-rated to be able to ensure that we are— our

03:24:58.118 --> 03:25:01.483
credit rating is good. And then we will look at market conditions and

03:25:01.983 --> 03:25:05.510
when it's the best time to move forward based on the solidification of all of

03:25:05.543 --> 03:25:08.447
that information. Um, uh,

03:25:08.752 --> 03:25:12.925
but with the passage of this bond resolution, we start the public process,

03:25:13.471 --> 03:25:16.680
and the council is envisioning that we will— that you'll be

03:25:17.180 --> 03:25:20.949
