04:29:22.572 --> 04:29:26.188
of dig through it, make any changes, have meetings, as much as you want,

04:29:26.526 --> 04:29:28.909
and then we have to have an adopted budget by the end of June,

04:29:29.021 --> 04:29:31.662
so we, and have our public hearings and things like that. Okay.

04:29:32.657 --> 04:29:36.494
I like to try to make sure we're touching on things as we come along,

04:29:37.008 --> 04:29:40.332
because the last thing we want is for you to get a budget in May

04:29:40.781 --> 04:29:43.832
that then has to be torn apart, or that doesn't feel like it's meeting the

04:29:44.332 --> 04:29:47.236
objectives and the vision of the council and what we want to do. So that

04:29:47.268 --> 04:29:50.608
was the— that's the purpose between kind of having

04:29:50.720 --> 04:29:54.494
these budget meetings, is we just kind of bite off chunks of some

04:29:54.994 --> 04:29:58.463
of these pieces, and we'll cover operations and personnel and we'll have a meeting

04:29:58.963 --> 04:30:02.643
where we talk about capital and things like that. And it's to try to make

04:30:03.143 --> 04:30:07.065
sure that we continue in the direction that the council is expecting for

04:30:07.565 --> 04:30:11.479
the upcoming year. So to be clear, let's go back on dates because right now

04:30:11.528 --> 04:30:14.939
we're planning on the personnel part on March 5th with our

04:30:15.069 --> 04:30:18.581
other, the special meeting, right? That's what we talked about?

04:30:19.593 --> 04:30:22.823
I think we— Isn't March 5th just the

04:30:23.323 --> 04:30:26.373
