could filibuster forever. When I say filibuster, 3 minutes at a time,

04:30:56.392 --> 04:30:59.826
different people. Right. I mean, depending on how many

04:30:59.842 --> 04:31:02.761
people show up, we would have to let all of them speak.

04:31:03.400 --> 04:31:06.832
But that's not any different than how we would do any public hearing. Mayor just

04:31:07.332 --> 04:31:09.959
jinxed us by saying it was going to be light. Well, we have a meeting

04:31:10.459 --> 04:31:12.141
on the 3rd, and then we're going to come back on the 5th and do

04:31:12.641 --> 04:31:15.795
it. What week is that? Thursday. It's on a Thursday.

04:31:15.941 --> 04:31:19.172
And if we plan— otherwise, we're not going to see her until

04:31:19.257 --> 04:31:22.717
when? So then you're— then we're looking at April,

04:31:22.990 --> 04:31:25.885
right? So yeah, so it makes sense to me to at least schedule it,

04:31:25.917 --> 04:31:29.038
to notice it, and to conduct it that way if there's time to do it.

04:31:29.456 --> 04:31:32.386
If we find that we're running 6 hours in a public hearing,

04:31:33.529 --> 04:31:36.250
I mean, at some point in time the mayor can call that and say we're

04:31:36.266 --> 04:31:39.567
